# Derived from docs/OWNERS.md — that file is the source of truth, this is a
# short, hand-synced excerpt covering only the high-friction areas.
#
# Replace @jason with the actual Gitea username before this has any effect.
#
# Gitea matches these patterns as REGULAR EXPRESSIONS over the full path (not
# gitignore-style globs like GitHub). Kept simple on purpose so that isn't a
# problem — no wildcards below.
#
# Gitea's CODEOWNERS only AUTO-ASSIGNS a reviewer; it has no equivalent of
# GitHub's "require review from Code Owners" branch-protection toggle. On
# Gitea this is a nudge, not a gate — the real gate is the "1 approval"
# branch-protection rule plus the PR template's scope checklist. (Except
# `platform/` itself, which has a REAL gate: `npm run framework:verify -- --check`
# in CI, hash-checked against platform/framework.lock whenever this repo's
# role is "consumer" — see docs/OWNERS.md and docs/DECISIONS.md.)
#
# One entry, not several: `platform/` already covers the shared UI library,
# AuthContext, and the auth service — all of them moved under it in the
# framework/app split.

platform/          @jason
src/theme.css      @jason
.claude/           @jason
